Z||000000||skitime||05-11-2001||11:28 AM||||I have tried the search and not finding the information I want.  I have a 88 GT t-top with an automatic and cruise. I bought a complete 88 GT 5 speed Getrag with engine, cradle, rear suspension, exhaust, pedals, clutch cylinder, shifter, shifting cables, steering column, ECM, and the entire car harness (The donor car had cruise too).  My questions:<BR>1. Will I have to install the wiring harness and if not what must I change electrically to convert to the 5 speed. I have the complete engine harness too of course.   <BR>2. Must I change ECM or can I plug the 5 speed engine harness into the auto ECM? <BR>3.I figured I would keep my original engine. Should I change the engine harnesses?<BR>4. Is changing the steering column necessary because of the "key removal when in park"?<BR>5. Is this worth the effort? I would like the 5 speed but do not want to mess the car up doing it. <BR>6.If I do not do the conversion what is this stuff worth. Engine 92,000 miles, Trans, Cradle and suspension.<P>Thanks and sorry for so many questions.<BR>||||reg||1
